n {:value "15"} "1960 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "16"} "1964 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "17"} "1968 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "18"} "1972 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "19"} "1976 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "20"} "1980 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "21"} "1984 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "22"} "1988 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "23"} "1992 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "24"} "1996 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "25"} "2000 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "26"} "2004 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "53"} "2008 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "65"} "2010 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "54"} "2012 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "67"} "2014 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "59"} "2016 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "69"} "2018 Summer Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "61"} "2020 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "63"} "2024 Summer Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/WRE'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Wrestling at the 1924 Summer Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "6 – 14 July 1924"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/266"} "Vélodrome d'Hiver, Paris"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "The Paris Olympics added three new events to the wrestling tournament. In the Greco-Roman style, a " [:a {:href "/results/121216"} "bantamweight division"] " was added, and some of the other weight limits were shuffled. Two new events were added to the freestyle competition, " [:a {:href "/results/121021"} "bantamweight"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/121104"} "welterweight"] ". This moved the " [:a {:href "/results/121193"} "heavyweight class"] " limit up to 87 kilogrammes."] "\n\n" [:p {} "For the Greco-Roman events, the tournament format was also changed: each wrestler remained in competition until he had lost two matches. Final order was decided based on the number of matches won. The freestyle events were conducted as single-elimination competition, with the Bergvall system used to determine the secondary medals. All those losing to the champion competed in the second-place tournament, and all those losing to the gold or silver medalist competed in a single-elimination third-place tournament. The match length was also slightly changed from " [:a {:href "/editions/7/sports/WRE"} "1920"] ": the fights were limited to 20 minutes, with ties going into overtime, a 6-minute ground wrestling decider."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The competitions saw a continued dominance of the Nordic nations in Greco-Roman wrestling, while the freestyle events were dominated by Switzerland and the United States. New in the Olympic wrestling arena was Japan, which was to become a dominant power in the sport several decades later. Through " [:a {:href "/athletes/59062"} "Katsutoshi Naito"] ", the Asian nation won its first wrestling medal. Wrestling was one of the sports conducted at the " [:a {:href "/venues/266"} "Vélodrome d’Hiver"] ", a single mat being located in the center field of the cycling track. The crowds were never big, with only a few hundred paying spectators attending each day."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/121216"} "Bantamweight, Greco-Roman (≤58 kg), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "6 – 10 July 1924"] "\n" [:td {} "25"] "\n" [:td {} "15"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/121268"